+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, but Narrowing the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. Like most rows, it was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Whether it was deliberate stayed open.
+
+On 2026-09-11 the owner requested narrowing the veterinarian list by specialty. The request read against the row as written: narrowing the list finds veterinarians by a criterion. The owner settled the conflict in the same request, recorded verbatim at intake:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the requested narrowing. Not chosen: the owner requested it.
+2. **Remove NG-9's veterinarian clause.** Open veterinarian search of every kind. Not chosen: the owner kept free-text veterinarian search out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined. Narrowing the directory by an attribute it already shows becomes in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed, not removed. Searching for a pet or a visit stays out of scope, and so does free-text searching for a veterinarian. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope. The first such narrowing is by specialty (`REQ-VET-003`).
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9's row in the PRD Non-Goals table carries the narrowed wording and links here.
+- A later request to narrow the directory by another shown attribute falls inside the row as narrowed. A request for free-text veterinarian search still needs its own recorded owner decision.
+- The pet and visit clauses of NG-9 are untouched and remain part of the open provenance consultation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the narrowing by specialty the row now admits.
